WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.366
The ocean absorbs a large share of humanity's
carbon emissions,

00:00:04.446 --> 00:00:10.365
yet our official picture of how much it takes up
always lags reality by about a year.

00:00:10.445 --> 00:00:16.082
This work introduces Carbon Monitor Ocean, or
CMO-NRT, a near-real-time, monthly,

00:00:16.162 --> 00:00:21.517
gridded dataset of global surface ocean fugacity of
CO2 and air-sea CO2 flux.

00:00:21.597 --> 00:00:27.939
By using convolutional neural networks and
semi-supervised learning to update the estimates

00:00:28.019 --> 00:00:32.245
from ten ocean biogeochemical models and eight data
products,

00:00:32.325 --> 00:00:36.832
the authors extend the global carbon budget to the
present month,

00:00:36.912 --> 00:00:42.690
giving scientists and policymakers a far more
timely view of the ocean carbon sink.
